  "stage": "synthesis-review",
  "summary": "The concise Year B Advent study passes source and local print review because Peter\u2019s need for grace and Jesus\u2019 need for his company, and Augustine\u2019s converted thief and Bellarmine\u2019s Christ born of Mary, remain distinct as in the expansive study, with the revised passages supported by Jerome XVII p. 158, Augustine on Psalm 79, Bede on Mark 13, Mark 13\u201314, Cyril XV and the U.S. bishops on the Collect. The ten-page proof places the twelve units and four senses on page 1, the chronology alone on page 2, the thematic argument on pages 3\u20134 and commentary from page 5, with the Mark 13:33\u201337 row locating Jesus\u2019 charge to watch on Mount Olivet opposite the Temple around A.D. 29 in Maas\u2019s chronology, marking the Passion date disputed and distinguishing it from composition in Rome or possibly Syria."
